{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-36155","model_call":40,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q157"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q157"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1523100517#3_3203893559","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q157","rank":5,"snippet":"34_1523100517#3_3203893559\" , \"end_char\": 3323.000000 , \"headings\": \"David Alfaro Siqueiros David Alfaro Siqueiros Learn More in these related Britannica articles: \" , \"segment\": \"Learn More in these related Britannica articles: Mexico: The arts > David Alfaro Siqueiros, depicting aspects of the Mexican Revolution, the country’s modernization, and <cover>class struggle, have become legendary. Orozco is also perhaps the most-popular of Mexico’s folk artists. His animated plaster-of-paris skeleton characters are both satirical and lifelike. Other notable artists include Nicolás Enríquez, Rufino… Latin American art: Populist art and the Mexican mural renaissance …of the Mexican muralists was David Alfaro Siqueiros. Devoting much of his time to union organizing and pamphleteering, Siqueiros was a fervent communist; </cover>as a result, his paintings are filled with highly simplified portrayals of proletarian masses. He embraced new industrial technology in his work and applied commercial materials such… Diego Rivera …meeting with fellow Mexican painter David Alfaro Siqueiros.\" , \"start_char\": 2429.000000 , \"title\": \"David Alfaro Siqueiros | Mexican painter | Britannica\" , \"url\":","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_1342511605#4_2485333648","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_1342511605#3_2485330599","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_105840807#11_118805216","rank":3,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_105840807#10_118802803","rank":4,"relevance":3}]},"time":7},"model_calls":40,"document_judgments":33,"relevance_3":23,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
